            <ArticleTitle>Coarctation of the aorta and cerebellar infarction: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>121-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 5-year-old child presented to our emergency department with a sudden onset of symptoms consistent with cerebellar infarction. Evaluation lead us to discover an undiagnosed coarctation of the aorta in association with a thrombotic cerebellar infarction. A review of coarctation follows.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
